I'm going to start with four things I personaly don't like about this game at all:
1) terrible in-game map layout (map – NOT level design), making treasure hunting really annoying at times;
2) leveling crafting jobs is a grinding nightmare;
3) pvp isn't fun at all;
4) the game constantly rubs the fact that it's an mmo in your face in the most annoying way imaginable which means sitting in queues forever for your mandatory storyline teamups with random people if you play as dps.
Bad things aside, they don't have much of an impact on overall game experience. Even considering all that, it's probably the best Final Fantasy game since FF X. There are many callbacks to old FF games too, from locations to boss fights and gear sets, yet none of those feel out of place. The game constantly gets updated with new content, events and patches, and Heavensward is an amazing expansion packed with so much stuff it's more of a sequel to A Realm Reborn than a mere addon. I think it's even more enjoyable than the "core" game. If you like Final Fantasy series and/or story-driven mmorpgs, you'll definitely have a good time with FF XIV.

